repository-code: "https://github.com/balkeumlabs/FedHet"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research artifact for a measured study of device-tier feature
  heterogeneity in federated health-risk scoring. Homes in a consumer edge-health
  deployment buy different hardware tiers and can therefore measure different
  biometrics, which breaks the shared-feature-space assumption of standard
  federated averaging. Using real NHANES survey data only, the artifact compares
  a centralized upper bound, intersection FedAvg, naive union FedAvg, and a
  tier-aware per-feature participation-weighted aggregation rule, and reports
  measured CPU time, RAPL package energy, and uplink bytes on a consumer CPU.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - feature heterogeneity
  - edge computing
  - digital health
  - NHANES
  - energy measurement
